The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
ret = kobject_init_and_add(&cpc_ptr->kobj, &cppc_ktype, &cpu_dev->kobj, "acpi_cppc");
if (ret) {
    per_cpu(cpc_desc_ptr, pr->id) = NULL;
    goto out_free;
}
```
Reason:
The function `kobject_init_and_add()` can fail, returning an error code. If it fails, the reference count of the kobject is not decremented because `kobject_put()` is not called, resulting in a memory leak as the allocated memory for the kobject is never freed.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
kobject_put(&cpc_ptr->kobj);
```
Reason:
Adding this call to `kobject_put()` ensures that when `kobject_init_and_add()` fails, the reference count is decremented appropriately, allowing the memory allocated for the kobject to be released and preventing the memory leak. This ensures proper cleanup when an error occurs.

